{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalRMatrixSubLemma","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.combinerValue_prod_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.combinerValue_prod_form","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OperatorValuedCombiner.lean#L134-L160","doc":"**Product-form convergence (conditional)** — the explicit telescoped form of\n`operator_valued_combiner_convergence`.  The `A = m + 2` combiner value is the\ndeuteron base case `combinerValue 2` multiplied by the running product of the\nLittlewood–Richardson weights `lrWeight (2 + j)`, `j = 0, …, m - 1`.  This is\nexactly the boxed product equation displayed in\n`prop:operator-valued-combiner-convergence`\n(`cv(2 + m) = (∏_{j=0}^{m-1} w(2 + j)) · cv(2)`); the companion theorem\n`operator_valued_combiner_convergence` states the same accumulation in the\nrecursive `iteratedCombinerValue` form.  Fully Lean-verified modulo the\n`[WenzlAOperator R q]` instance hypothesis (the §3b-cond conjecture). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.operator_valued_combiner_convergence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.operator_valued_combiner_convergence","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OperatorValuedCombiner.lean#L111-L132","doc":"**Convergence at every level ≥ 2 (conditional)** — the iterated application\nof the branching recursion assembles into a convergent representation.\nThis proves `prop:operator-valued-combiner-convergence` using `Nat.rec`,\nestablishing that the `A`-nucleon value is exactly the unwound\naccumulation from the `A=2` base case. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:operator-valued-combiner-convergence","label":"prop:operator-valued-combiner-convergence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/operator-valued-combiner-convergence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.iteratedCombinerValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.iteratedCombinerValue","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OperatorValuedCombiner.lean#L102-L109","doc":"Unwinds the branching recursion using `Nat.rec`.\nAt step `n`, computes the `A = n + 2` combiner value by multiplying the\nLR weight `lrWeight (n + 1)` with the previously computed value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.combiner_value_three_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.combiner_value_three_eq","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OperatorValuedCombiner.lean#L83-L100","doc":"**`prop:operator-valued-combiner-convergence` (conditional)** — the\nA=3 (tritium / ³He) combiner value is the LR-weighted A=2 value.\n\nFully Lean-verified modulo the `[WenzlAOperator R q]` instance\nhypothesis (the conjecture).  This is the first nontrivial unwinding\nof the branching recursion: the 9-strand atomic χ-value is built\nfrom the 6-strand (deuteron) base case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.branching_recursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.branching_recursion","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OperatorValuedCombiner.lean#L78-L78","doc":"**The convergence recursion** (the conjecture's content): for every\natomic level `A ≥ 2`, the combiner value at `A+1` equals the\nLR-weighted combiner.\n\n**Gap Analysis:** The in-repo RSK infrastructure (`QOU.Mathlib.RSK_substrate_proved`) provides\nthe classical Burnside identity, but this convergence requires universal extracts for H_9+\nwhich are not covered by standard RSK. This remains an open research-grade gap.\n\nBottoms out at A=2 (deuteron), verified\nnumerically at 0.72 ppb (Phase A). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.lrWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.lrWeight","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OperatorValuedCombiner.lean#L67-L67","doc":"Littlewood–Richardson weight for the peel level A → A+1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.combinerValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.combinerValue","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OperatorValuedCombiner.lean#L65-L65","doc":"χ-value of the operator-valued combiner at peel level A (= 3A strands). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OperatorValuedCombiner.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.OperatorValuedCombiner.WenzlAOperator","kind":"class","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/OperatorValuedCombiner.lean#L49-L79","doc":"**§3b-cond conjectural class**: the operator-valued Wenzl branching\ncombiner.\n\n`combinerValue A` is the χ-value the combiner produces for the\ncanonical A-nucleon atomic braid (at H_{3A}).  `lrWeight A` is the\nLittlewood–Richardson weight entering the peel from level A to\nlevel A+1.  The `branching_recursion` field is the convergence\ncontent of `prop:operator-valued-combiner-convergence`: the\nvalue at each level ≥ 2 is determined from the previous by the\nLR-weighted combiner.\n\nNo instance is provided — the missing instance is the conjecture\n(universal H_9+ extracts, research-grade). ","signatureChunk":0}]}